sentences.t:
Lo que yo dixier[o] non lo tengades a mal:
en Castejón non podriemos fincar;
çerca es el rey Alfonsso e buscar nos verná.

sentences.l:
What I may-say not it hold-you to ill:
in Castejón not we-could remain;
near is the king Alfonsso and to-seek us he-will-come.

sentences.t:
Mas el castiello non lo quiero hermar;
çiento moros e çiento moras quiero las [i] quitar,
por que lo pris dellos que de mí non digan mal.

sentences.l:
But the castle not it I-want to-lay-waste;
a-hundred Moors and a-hundred Moorish-women I-want them [there] to-free,
so that, since it I-took from-them, that of me not they-say ill.

sentences.t:
Lo que dixo el Çid a todos los otros plaz.
Del castiello que prisieron todos ricos se parten;
los moros e las moras bendiziéndol están.

sentences.l:
What said the Çid to all the others pleases.
From-the castle that they-took all rich themselves depart;
the Moors and the Moorish-women blessing-him are.

sentences.t:
e sobre Alcoçer mio Çid iva posar,
en un otero redondo, fuerte e grand;
açerca corre Salón, agua nol puedent vedar.

sentences.l:
and over Alcoçer my Çid went to-camp,
on a hill round, strong and great;
near runs Salón, water not-him they-can forbid.
